#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:2
msgid "Documentation in scientific and academic publishing"
msgstr "科学与学术出版中的文档"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:4
msgid ""
"On this page, we explore some of the many tools and practices that "
"*software* documentation and *academic* writing share. If you are working "
"within the field of science or academia, this page can be used as an "
"introduction."
msgstr "本页探讨*软件* 文档与*学术* 写作共有的诸多工具和实践。若你在科学或学术领域工作，本页可作为入门介绍。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:23
msgid ""
"Documentation and technical writing are broad fields. Their tools and "
"practices have grown relevant to most scientific activities. This includes "
"building publications, books, educational resources, interactive data "
"science, resources for data journalism and full-scale websites for research "
"projects and courses."
msgstr "文档和技术写作是宽泛的领域，其工具和实践已与大多数科学活动相关。这包括构建出版物、书籍、教学资源、交互式数据科学、数据新闻报道资源，以及为研究项目和课程构建的完整网站。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:27
msgid ""
"Here's a brief overview of some :doc:`features </reference/features>` that "
"people in science and academic writing love about Read the Docs:"
msgstr "以下是科学与学术写作领域用户喜爱的 Read the Docs 部分 :doc:`功能 </reference/features>` 简介："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst
msgid "🪄 Easy to use"
msgstr "🪄 易于使用"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:32
msgid ""
"Documentation code doesn't have to be written by a programmer. In fact, "
"documentation coding languages are designed and developed so you don't have "
"to be a programmer, and there are many writing aids that makes it easy to "
"abstract from code and focus on content."
msgstr "文档代码不必由程序员编写。事实上，文档编写语言的设计和开发初衷就是让你无需成为程序员也能使用，并且有诸多写作辅助工具让你能轻松从代码中抽离、专注于内容。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:34
msgid "Getting started is also made easy:"
msgstr "入门同样轻松："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:36
msgid ""
"All new to this? Take the official :external+jupyterbook:doc:`Jupyter Book "
"Tutorial <start/your-first-book>`"
msgstr ""
"对此完全陌生？阅读官方 :external+jupyterbook:doc:`Jupyter Book 教程 <start/your-first-"
"book>`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:37
msgid "Curious for practical code? See :doc:`/examples`"
msgstr "想看实用代码？参见 :doc:`/examples`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:38
msgid "Familiar with Sphinx? See :doc:`/guides/jupyter`"
msgstr "熟悉 Sphinx？参见 :doc:`/guides/jupyter`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst
msgid "🔋 Batteries included: Graphs, computations, formulas, maps, diagrams and more"
msgstr "🔋 开箱即用：图表、计算、公式、地图、示意图等"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:42
msgid ""
"Take full advantage of getting all the richness of "
":external+jupyter:doc:`Jupyter Notebook <index>` combined with Sphinx and "
"the giant ecosystem of extensions for both of these."
msgstr ""
"充分结合 :external+jupyter:doc:`Jupyter Notebook <index>` 的丰富能力与 "
"Sphinx，以及两者庞大的扩展生态。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:44
msgid "Here are some examples:"
msgstr "以下是一些示例："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:46
msgid ""
"Use symbols familiar from math and physics, build advanced proofs. See also:"
" `sphinx-proof <https://sphinx-"
"proof.readthedocs.io/en/latest/syntax.html>`__"
msgstr ""
"使用数学和物理中熟悉的符号，编写高级证明。另见：`sphinx-proof <https://sphinx-"
"proof.readthedocs.io/en/latest/syntax.html>`__"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:47
msgid ""
"Present results with plots, graphs, images and let users interact directly "
"with your datasets and algorithms. See also: `Matplotlib "
"<https://matplotlib.org/stable/tutorials/introductory/usage.html>`__, "
"`Interactive Data Visualizations "
"<https://jupyterbook.org/en/stable/interactive/interactive.html>`__"
msgstr ""
"用图表、曲线、图片呈现结果，让用户直接与你的数据集和算法交互。另见：`Matplotlib "
"<https://matplotlib.org/stable/tutorials/introductory/usage.html>`__ "
"、`Interactive Data Visualizations "
"<https://jupyterbook.org/en/stable/interactive/interactive.html>`__"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:48
msgid ""
"Graphs, tables etc. are computed when the latest version of your project is "
"built and published as a stand-alone website. All code examples on your "
"website are validated each time you build."
msgstr "图表、表格等在构建项目最新版本时计算生成，并发布为独立网站。你网站上的所有代码示例在每次构建时都会得到验证。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst
msgid "📚 Bibliographies and external links"
msgstr "📚 参考文献与外部链接"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:52
msgid ""
"Maintain bibliography databases directly as code and have external links "
"automatically verified."
msgstr "直接以代码方式维护参考文献数据库，并自动验证外部链接。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:54
msgid ""
"Using extensions for Sphinx such as the popular `sphinxcontrib-bibtex <https"
"://sphinxcontrib-bibtex.readthedocs.io/>`__ extension, you can maintain your"
" bibliography with Sphinx directly or refer to entries ``.bib`` files, as "
"well as generating entire Bibliography sections from those files."
msgstr ""
"使用 Sphinx 扩展（如流行的 `sphinxcontrib-bibtex <https://sphinxcontrib-"
"bibtex.readthedocs.io/>`__ 扩展），你可以直接用 Sphinx 维护参考文献，或引用 ``.bib`` "
"文件中的条目，还能从这些文件生成完整的参考文献章节。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst
msgid "📜 Modern themes and classic PDF outputs"
msgstr "📜 现代主题与经典 PDF 输出"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:61
msgid ""
"Use the latest state-of-the-art themes for web and have PDFs and e-book "
"formats automatically generated."
msgstr "网页使用最新的前沿主题，PDF 和电子书格式自动生成。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:63
msgid ""
"New themes are improving every day, and when you write documentation based "
"on Jupyter Book and Sphinx, you will separate your contents and semantics "
"from your presentation logic. This way, you can keep up with the latest "
"theme updates or try new themes."
msgstr ""
"新主题每天都在改进。基于 Jupyter Book 和 Sphinx "
"编写文档时，你会将内容与语义同展示逻辑分离。这样既能跟上最新主题更新，也能尝试新主题。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:65
msgid ""
"Another example of the benefits from separating content and presentation "
"logic: Your documentation also transforms into printable books and eBooks."
msgstr "内容与展示逻辑分离的另一个好处示例：你的文档还能转换为可打印的书籍和电子书。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst
msgid "📐 Widgets, widgets and more widgets"
msgstr "📐 组件、组件，还有更多组件"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:69
msgid ""
"Design your science project's layout and components with widgets from a rich"
" eco-system of open-source extensions built for many purposes. Special "
"widgets help users display and interact with graphs, maps and more. "
":external+jupyterbook:doc:`Several <content/components>` `extensions <https"
"://sphinx-gallery.github.io/>`__ are built and invented by the science "
"community."
msgstr ""
"用来自丰富开源扩展生态的组件设计科学项目的布局，这些扩展用途多样。专门的组件可帮助用户展示并与图表、地图等交互。:external+jupyterbook:doc:`多个"
" <content/components>` `扩展 <https://sphinx-gallery.github.io/>`__ "
"由科学社区构建和发明。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst
msgid "⚙️ Automatic builds"
msgstr "⚙️ 自动构建"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:73
msgid ""
"Build and publish your project for every change made through Git (GitHub, "
"GitLab, Bitbucket etc). Preview changes via pull requests. Receive "
"notifications when something is wrong. How does this work? Have a look at "
"this video:"
msgstr ""
"每次通过 Git（GitHub、GitLab、Bitbucket 等）做出更改时自动构建并发布项目。通过 Pull Request "
"预览变更。出现问题时收到通知。这如何运作？观看此视频："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst
msgid "💬 Collaboration and community"
msgstr "💬 协作与社区"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:89
msgid ""
"Science and academia have a big kinship with software developers: We ❤️ "
"community. Our solutions and projects become better when we foster "
"inclusivity and active participation. Read the Docs features easy access for"
" readers to suggest changes via your git platform (GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket"
" etc.). But not just any unqualified feedback. Instead, the *code* and all "
"the tools are available for your community to forge qualified contributions."
msgstr ""
"科学与学术界与软件开发者有深厚的亲缘关系：我们热爱社区 ❤️。当我们促进包容性和积极参与时，我们的方案和项目会变得更好。Read the Docs "
"让读者可通过你的 git 平台（GitHub、GitLab、Bitbucket "
"等）便捷地提出修改建议。但并非任何无资质的反馈——你的社区可以使用*代码* 及所有工具，产出有价值的贡献。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:91
msgid "Your readers can become your co-authors!"
msgstr "你的读者可以成为你的合著者！"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:93
msgid ""
"Discuss changes via pull request and track all changes in your project's "
"version history."
msgstr "通过 Pull Request 讨论变更，并在项目的版本历史中追踪所有更改。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:95
msgid ""
"Using git does not mean that anyone can go and change your code and your "
"published project. The full ownership and permission handling remains in "
"your hands. Project and organization owners on your git platform govern what"
" is released and who has access to approve and build changes."
msgstr ""
"使用 git 并不意味着任何人都能随意更改你的代码和已发布项目。完整的所有权和权限管理仍在你手中。你的 git "
"平台上的项目和组织所有者决定发布内容，以及谁有权批准和构建变更。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst
msgid "🔎 Full search and analytics"
msgstr "🔎 完整搜索与分析"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:99
msgid ""
"Read the Docs comes with a number of features bundled in that you would have"
" to configure if you were hosting documentation elsewhere."
msgstr "Read the Docs 自带若干功能，若你在其他地方托管文档则需自行配置。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:101
msgid "Super-fast text search"
msgstr "极速全文搜索"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:102
msgid "Your documentation is automatically indexed and gets its own search function."
msgstr "你的文档会自动建立索引，并拥有自己的搜索功能。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:104
msgid "Traffic statistics"
msgstr "流量统计"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:105
msgid ""
"Have full access to your traffic data and have quick access to see which of "
"your pages are most popular."
msgstr "完整访问你的流量数据，快速查看哪些页面最受欢迎。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:107
msgid "Search analytics"
msgstr "搜索分析"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:108
msgid ""
"What are people searching for and do they get hits? From each search query "
"in your documentation, we collect a neat little statistic that can help to "
"improve the discoverability and relevance of your documentation."
msgstr "人们在搜索什么？是否找到了结果？我们从文档中的每次搜索查询收集一项有用的小统计，可帮助你改进文档的可发现性和相关性。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:110
msgid "SEO - Don't reinvent search engine optimization"
msgstr "SEO——不必重新发明搜索引擎优化"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:111
msgid ""
"Use built-in SEO best-practices from Sphinx, its themes and Read the Docs "
"hosting. This can give you a good ranking on search engines as a direct "
"outcome of simply writing and publishing your documentation project."
msgstr "利用 Sphinx、其主题和 Read the Docs 托管内置的 SEO 最佳实践。仅仅编写并发布你的文档项目，就能直接带来不错的搜索引擎排名。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst
msgid "🌱 Grow your own solutions"
msgstr "🌱 培育你自己的方案"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:115
msgid ""
"The eco-system is open source and makes it accessible for anyone with Python"
" skills to build their own extensions."
msgstr "该生态是开源的，任何具备 Python 技能的人都可以构建自己的扩展。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:117
msgid ""
"We want science communities to use Read the Docs and to be part of the "
"documentation community 💞"
msgstr "我们希望科学社区使用 Read the Docs，并成为文档社区的一员 💞"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/science.rst:120
